#
# tests/golden/provider-adapter-openapi.v7.json is a pinned snapshot of the
# integration provider's public flat-v7 OpenAPI contract (provider commit
# b2745459). Its test asserts two pins:
#   * transport pin -- SHA-256 of the exact bytes, which must equal the digest
#     of the provider's own blob (7a484f39...) so the baseline is independently
#     verifiable against provider source rather than against whoever's checkout
#     recorded it;
#   * semantic pin -- a content-canonical (parsed, sorted-key) digest.
#
# The provider stores that contract with LF endings. This repository is
# developed on Windows where `core.autocrlf = true` and validated in CI on
# Linux, so WITHOUT the `-text` rule below git would rewrite this file to CRLF
# on a Windows checkout. That silently changes its bytes, changes the transport
# pin from 7a484f39... to 4b3830bc..., and makes the golden test report drift
# against the provider that does not actually exist.
#
# `-text` therefore means: git must never perform end-of-line conversion on this
# file in either direction. It is a deliberate correctness control, not an
# oversight or a stray inconsistency. If a repository-wide normalization rule
# (e.g. `* text=auto`) is introduced later, this exemption must be preserved
# ahead of it; normalizing this file WILL break the pin.
tests/golden/provider-adapter-openapi.v7.json -text
